From ef4cc66f36d958ae817af6fe6385d8c351a8f56d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GPenG Chen <302976981@qq.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 07:11:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] audio: tinyalsa_hal: add es8311 sound card support
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The RK3576 board uses an ES8311 codec. The tinyalsa primary HAL did not
recognize the "rockchipes8311" ALSA card name, so the speaker card number
stayed -1 (SND_OUT_SOUND_CARD_UNKNOWN) and every playback attempt failed
with "route_pcm_card_open() card -1 error!" — no sound from the system.

- Register "rockchipes8311" in SPEAKER_OUT_NAME / MIC_IN_NAME so both
  playback and capture map to the card.
- Add an es8311 codec route table and register it in config_list.h.
  The new es8311 driver (kernel-6.1) has no "Playback Path" enum: the
  codec path is pure DAPM (I2S IN -> MONO DAC -> DIFFERENTIAL OUT) and
  the PA is enabled by the machine driver's DAPM event, so the table
  only pins DAC/ADC VOLUME at 0 dB (191 of 0~255).

Change-Id: Iec30157848b80b23257eba0acef8a4d1782a8998
---
 tinyalsa_hal/audio_hw.c                   |   2 +
 tinyalsa_hal/codec_config/config_list.h   |   5 +
 tinyalsa_hal/codec_config/es8311_config.h | 300 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 307 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 tinyalsa_hal/codec_config/es8311_config.h

